<title>UK: UK hostile to fudged single currency, says Clarke.</title>
<headline>UK hostile to fudged single currency, says Clarke.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Wednesday the government was against the idea of blurring the entry criteria for countries wishing to enter a single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;We are hostile to a fudged single currency. We are hostile to anybody else going ahead with a fudged single currency,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
</text>
